          {
            "text": "A former social worker, she managed justice reform at Business and Professional People for the Public Interest and the state's Adult Redeploy Illinois program.",
            "cites": [2]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "She supports a progressive state tax system to reduce the burden on working families. She criticized a proposed $40 million cut to the state homelessness budget. A law she sponsored created an alternative to the social work licensing exam. She introduced legislation encouraging behavioral health providers to join commercial insurance networks. Another law she sponsored guarantees universal mental health screenings for public school students. She helped secure $13 million for an older-adult shelter on the Far Northwest Side.",
